:eb26a040daf9b882557c71e875e9e002","name":"SCHOOL.DISTRICT.27.OFFICES","operator":"NYC Department of Education","category":"government-offices","subcategory":"OFFICE LEASED BY EDUC","is_coad_member":false,"lon":-73.85818,"lat":40.684508,"address":"82-01 Rockaway Boulevard, Ozone Park, 11416","source":"facdb","provenance":"dcp_facilities_database","verified_on":"8/28/26"},{"resource_id":"qnpd:alphapointe","name":"Alphapointe","category":"benefits-and-legal","subcategory":"Workforce Development","is_coad_member":false,"lon":-73.826964,"lat":40.699112,"address":"87-46 123rd Street Richmond Hill, NY 11418","mission":"Alphapointe is a nonprofit organization dedicated to empowering people with vision loss by providing employment opportunities, job training, and rehabilitation services. We are one of the largest employers of people who are blind and visually impaired in the U.S. We combine comprehensive rehabilitation services, advocacy, and community involvement to help people achieve independence and success in the workplace and home. Our mission is to empower people with vision loss to achieve their goals and aspirations. One of the most important ways we serve those with vision loss is to help them understand that sight loss isn't a barrier to potential. We use our mission and vision as guides to lead us forward, to make sure every decision, every action, and every move meets our end goal of serving those with vision loss to the best of our abilities.","contact_name":"Mark D'Altorio","email":"mDaltorio@alphapointe.org","phone":"718.854.7300","website":"alphapointe.org","social":"Facebook: @alphapointeny; Twitter: @alphapointe; YouTube: @alphapointeonline","languages":"English, Spanish, Chinese","accepts_referrals":"Yes","fees":"None","source":"qnpd","provenance":"queens_nonprofit_directory_v3","verified_on":"8/28/26"},{"resource_id":"qnpd:center-for-the-women-of-new-york--1","name":"Center for the Women of New York","category":"benefits-and-legal","subcategory":"Gender