a nonprofit 501(c)(3) organization dedicated to the equality, advancement, and wellbeing of women.","contact_name":"Cecilia Venosta-Wiygul","email":"ceciliavenosta@cwny.org","phone":"718.793.0672","website":"cwny.org","social":"Facebook: @centerwomenny; Twitter/X: @centerwomenNY; LinkedIn: @Center for the Women of New York; Instagram: @centerwomenny","languages":"English, Spanish","accepts_referrals":"Yes","fees":"None","source":"qnpd","provenance":"queens_nonprofit_directory_v3","verified_on":"8/28/26"},{"resource_id":"qnpd:cidny-ny-connects","name":"CIDNY NY Connects","category":"benefits-and-legal","subcategory":"Human Services & Social Services","is_coad_member":false,"lon":-73.831369,"lat":40.713569,"address":"80-02 Kew Gardens Rd, Ste 400, Kew Gardens, NY 11415","mission":"CIDNY's NY Connects program is a free, trusted place to go for information about services and resources that support people with disabilities. We work with New Yorkers of all ages and with any type of disability whether they live at home, in a nursing home, or another residential setting.","contact_name":"Karline Balan","email":"Kbalan@cidny.org","phone":"646.849.8319","website":"cidny.org","languages":"English, Spanish, Haitian Creole, Mandarin,","accepts_referrals":"Yes","fees":"None","source":"qnpd","provenance":"queens_nonprofit_directory_v3","verified_on":"8/28/26"},{"resource_id":"qnpd:friends-of-maple-grove-cemetery-inc","name":"Friends of Maple Grove Cemetery inc .","category":"libraries-and-community","subcategory":"Arts & Culture","is_coad_member":false,"lon":-73.824149,"lat":40.707222,"address":"127-15 Kew Gardens Road, Kew Gardens, NY 11415","mission":"Established in 2005, the Friends of Maple Grove, Inc. is a nonprofit membership organization dedicated to supporting and enriching the operations of Maple Grove Cemetery in Kew Gardens, Queens. Our mission is to honor, memorialize, and celebrate life while fostering appreciation of the cemetery's artistic, historical, horticultural, and cultural treasures. Guided by our motto, \"Where History Comes Alive,\" we highlight the stories of the 117,000 individuals cared for at Maple Grove while preserving its beauty and tranquility for future generations.","contact_name":"Carl Ballenas","email":"carl.ballenas@gmail.com","phone":"646.229.2455","website":"friendsofmaplegrove.org","social":"Facebook: @FriendsOfMapleGroveCemetery; Instagram: @historicmaplegrove","languages":"English","accepts_referrals":"Yes","fees":"Some services have a small charge.","source":"qnpd","provenance":"queens_nonprofit_directory_v3","verified_on":"8/28/26"},{"resource_id":"qnpd:latin-american-intercultural-alliance","name":"Latin American Intercultural Alliance","category":"libraries-and-community","subcategory":"Arts & Culture","is_coad_member":false,"lon":-73.838819,"lat":40.697601,"address":"86-28 110th Street, Richmond Hill, NY 11418","mission":"Advocacy for Immigrant, Women and LGBTQ+ Rights, Mental Health, Literacy, Arts & Culture and Health & Wellness.","contact_name":"Rubén Cruz","email":"rubencruz@duck.com","phone":"347.995.2744","website":"jurukan.wixsite.com/laia/about","social":"Facebook: @LAIAinternacional","languages":"English and Spanish","accepts_referrals":"Yes","fees":"None","source":"qnpd","provenance":"queens_nonprofit_directory_v3","verified_on":"8/28/26"},{"resource_id":"qnpd:outreach-development-corporation-outreach","name":"Outreach Development Corporation (Outreach)","category":"health-care","subcategory":"Substance Abuse","is_coad_member":false,"lon":-73.831966,"lat":40.70028,"address":"117-11 Myrtle Avenue, Richmond Hill, NY 11418","mission":"To inspire individuals and families to achieve a life of unlimited potential.","contact_name":"Thanh Pham","email":"thanhpham@opiny.org","phone":"929.712.5829","website":"opiny.org","social":"Facebook: @Outreach: Building Healthy Lives; Instagram: @outreachny","languages":"English, Spanish, Polish","accepts_referrals":"Yes","fees":"Insurance or sliding scale","source":"qnpd","provenance":"queens_nonprofit_directory_v3","verified_on":"8/28/26"},{"resource_id":"qnpd:richmond-hill-historical-society","name":"Richmond Hill Historical Society","category":"libraries-and-community","subcategory":"Education","is_coad_member":false,"lon":-73.838638,"lat":40.702575,"address":"112-13 84th Avenue, Richmond Hill, NY 11418","mission":"We are a not-for-profit organization devoted to preserving the rich history of Richmond Hill. We promote the historic heritage of our architectural legacy and the contributions of our past and present residents through educational lectures, research, and participation in local historical events. We promote historic plaques for residences and archive records and personal collections which are available to researchers.","contact_name":"Helen Day","email":"richmond.hill.historical@gmail.com","phone":"262.686.7447 (RHHS General Number)","website":"richmondhillhistory.org","social":"Facebook: @Richmond Hill Historical Society","languages":"English","accepts_referrals":"Yes","fees":"None","source":"qnpd","provenance":"queens_nonprofit_directory_v3","verified_on":"8/28/26"},{"resource_id":"qnpd:school-sisters-of-notre-dame-educational-center--1","name":"School Sisters of Notre Dame Educational Center","category":"libraries-and-community","subcategory":"Education","is_coad_member":false,"lon":-73.856384,"lat":40.690952,"address":"87-04 88th Ave, Woodhaven, NY 11421","mission":"We believe an educated woman is the agent of change for herself, her family, and society. We serve women whose opportunities for education have been limited by circumstances. The School Sisters of Notre Dame Educational Center, Inc., located in Woodhaven, NY, empowers underserved women of all races and faiths to reach the fullness of their potential. Services: ESOL, GED, Citizenship Preparation, Digital Literacy.","contact_name":"Francine Poppo","email":"francine.poppo@ssndecwomens.org","phone":"516.314.4320","website":"ssndecwomens.org"